      "instagramProfileUrl": "https://www.instagram.com/roni.kordis/",
      "postCaption": "For a long time, TIAN Restaurant Wien had been at the very top of my list of restaurants to visit. Awarded one Michelin star, TIAN is something truly unique. It serves exclusively vegetarian and vegan cuisine - still a rarity in the world of Michelin-starred dining. When I finally managed to get a reservation, I drove to Vienna. I have to admit, I arrived with a bit of skepticism. Austrian cuisine wasn't something I knew well, and the stereotypes I had in mind didn't exactly make me expect an unforgettable plant-based dining experience. Sometimes, though, the best thing you can do is simply go with the flow. I certainly wasn't disappointed. The restaurant was completely full, yet the service was flawless from start to finish. More importantly, every course exceeded my expectations. Dish after dish, I found myself surprised by the creativity, the precision, and the incredible flavours. Every bite was a reminder that vegetables, grains, herbs, and fruits can be just as exciting as any other ingredient when they're treated with imagination and respect. If you follow a vegetarian or vegan lifestyle, TIAN is an absolute must-visit. The eight-course vegan tasting menu cost €189, and it was worth every euro. #TIAN #Vienna #Austria #MichelinStar #MichelinGuide #FineDining #VeganFineDining #PlantBased #Vegetarian #VeganTravel #Foodie #SustainableDining #LuxuryTravel #TravelAndTaste #CulinaryExperience",
